			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://hachyderm.io/@dylanbeattie\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>dylanbeattie</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fosstodon.org/@chris_hayes\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>chris_hayes</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> <br>In basic just inform the Rockstar developers to follow the steps from the Linkedin documentation to add a certification to your Linkedin profile, with for example Certified Rockstar Developer.<br>The only thing to get this active, you have to connect it to a \"company\"-page on Linkedin.</p><p>For fun you can add form to the Rockstar website, where the developers can answer a \"question\" to get the certification. 😆 . Zach created suchs as well <a href=\"https://www.11ty.dev/blog/certification/\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" translate=\"no\" target=\"_blank\"><span class=\"invisible\">https://www.</span><span class=\"\">11ty.dev/blog/certification/</span><span class=\"invisible\"></span></a></p>",
